 of all of humanity like  Alaska's sovereign wealth fund which  delivers a percentage of oil revenue to  its residents the same could be done for  the inhabitants of planet Earth  yes compensate the companies in  solved in the extraction but distribute  the wealth in a manner that reflects a  democratic vision of outer space if we  choose to see the space beyond earth as  an International Commons it would give  us a fantastic opportunity to experiment  with redistribute of mechanisms beyond  the usual confines of nation-states if  we can think big picture and establish a  sovereign wealth fund for the entire  earth imagine what that could do for our  species and the planet as space resource  extraction grows and becomes a more  profitable industry redistribution of  the revenue could create a genuine  global universal basic income freeing  citizens the world over from crippling  poverty elevating developing nations and  furthering the advancement of the entire  species the windfall from space industry  could allow nations to invest in clean  energy public works programs education  and their own space programs easing the  burden on the already existing ones a  super abundance of resources like  platinum that are scarce here on earth  could potentially allow for an expansion  of automation to the extent that output  is dramatically increased in the need  for human labour reduced allowing all  people more time to spend with their  loved ones and pursue things like the  arts which benefit everyone there's  nothing wrong with making money from  space resources as long as that money is  distributed equitably now is the time to  start talking about the democratization  about her space either it benefits  everyone or we're headed for a dystopia  of inequality we cannot yet begin to  fathom outer space shouldn't be about  flag-waving and conquest but about the  expansion of human potential beyond the  bounds of earth in a way that elevates  all of us if you'd like to learn more  about some of the upcoming private space  missions I highly recommend you check  out packing for Mars on curiosity stream  it's a fascinating look at all the  challenges involved in landing humans on  the red planet if you watch my videos  you'll know I'm a big fan of curiosity  stream it's an online streaming service  with thousands of nonfiction titles from  some of the best filmmakers in the game  you can find tons of great episodes like  packing for Mars and they've got a bunch  of material on technology and outer  space which are some of my favorites  they're giant catalogue includes content  on science nature astronomy technology  and lifestyle among others curiosity  stream has always supported independent  content creators so they've partnered  with nebula the streaming platform built  by a bunch of your favorite youtubers  including me nebula is a place for us to  try new things and make original content  that just wouldn't be possible on  YouTube it's a home for all of your  favorite creators outside of YouTube and  there's a ton of cool original  tent already there with more on the way  you can get unlimited access to both  curiosity stream and nebula for just 20  bucks a year that's less than two  dollars a month and it really does help  me create more content like this give  curiosity stream a shot visit curiosity  stream comm slash second thought if you  enjoyed this video and you'd like to see  more like it consider subscribing to  stay up to date with my latest episodes  if you hated it go ahead and drop a  thumbs down and if you really want to  help support my channel I recently  started a patreon which you can find at  patreon.com slash second thought you can  check out my previous episodes by  clicking the links on your screen thanks  for watching and I'll see you next week

